  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Health Systems in Afghanistan - Afghanistan (01-Apr-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan, RSSH, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Afghanistan)This program has the following goals: Strengthening the health system to reduce mortality and morbidity associated with ATM and RMNCH. The objectives of this program are: To ensure quality implementation of the Community Health Nursing Education program in rural areas of Afghanistan to increase access to community-based health care services targeting HIV/AIDS, tuberculosis and malaria.  To improve the data quality of the HMIS information and strengthen the utilization of data for decision-making at all levels.  To maintain and improve quality of Regional Reference Laboratories network</narrative>
  </description>
